#+TITLE: COM runtime can overtake asynchronous EPURE SCRIPT startup
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation

* Evidence
MR !507 job17673570646 verifies the exact BricsCAD job DWG but both EPURE
APIs are absent. The bridge dispatches SCRIPT and the runtime LOAD as
separate SendCommand calls. A single-line SCRIPT wrapper does not fix it
(job17673828953), so parsing the control file alone is not the cause.

* Correction under qualification
COM loads EPURE in :run-common-prelude, on the same Lisp stack as the
bootstrap, before entering the protocol server loop. Batch remains unchanged.
The regression fails4/6 checks before the correction and passes6/6 after it.
The related launcher tests pass on SBCL and CCL. Require native proof before
closing: both EPURE APIs, correct DWG and clean owned process termination.

** Native document-startup evidence (2026-11-02)
Synchronous control loading alone left BricsCAD APIs absent. Profile selection
after Documents.Open does not replay on_start.lsp/S::STARTUP. Running the real
installed entry point when com_startup_exe is nil restores both APIs in the
exact job DWG under a cold BricsCAD profile. A cold AutoCAD profile likewise
needs AcadDoc.lsp/S::STARTUP; this restores both APIs. Shutdown qualification
remains open separately: AutoCAD returns BABE variants and earlier real AVs.
Failed experimental generic shutdown changes are excluded from this fix.
